    'founder.lead':'Matodzi Makananisa is the founder of <b>Streaming on F.A.M.E</b>. Since 2015 — when the F.A.M.E brand first launched as an entertainment awards platform — Matodzi has been building toward a single vision: to <b>entertain and empower Africa</b>.',
    'founder.p1':'Under his leadership, F.A.M.E is producing original "Black Power" shows that give young people the tools to confront unemployment, start businesses and create jobs in their own communities. The streaming service is projected to create approximately <b>300 jobs</b> in its first financial year, with the broader TV and film production value chain set to benefit.',
    'founder.p2':'Matodzi describes F.A.M.E\'s philosophy plainly: <em>"Pay off line is Black Power."</em> It\'s a statement of intent — that entertainment, done right, can be a vehicle for economic empowerment across the continent.',
