    'faq.q1':'What is Streaming on F.A.M.E?','faq.a1':'South Africa\'s home of local entertainment. F.A.M.E is a mobile-first video-on-demand platform bringing together African originals, series, movies, documentaries, reality, kids content, music and live events — at an affordable monthly price.',
    'faq.q2':'When does it launch?','faq.a2':'Our target is a full public launch on <b>1 June 2027</b>, following a development window from October 2026 to February 2027. Waitlist members get access first.',
    'faq.q3':'How much does it cost?','faq.a3':'Two plans: <b>R29.90/month</b> (ad-supported) and <b>R39.90/month</b> (ad-less experience). No hidden fees, no contracts, cancel anytime.',
    'faq.q4':'What can I watch on Streaming on F.A.M.E?','faq.a4':'Reality TV, animations, documentaries, series, movies, music videos, short films, live events, kids content and educational programming — with a strong focus on African originals.',
    'faq.q5':'What devices are supported?','faq.a5':'At launch: mobile web (PWA) and the Android app. Phase two adds iOS, desktop web and Smart TV apps. Smart downloads and offline viewing are supported on mobile.',
    'faq.q6':'Is there any commitment when signing up?','faq.a6':'None at all. There are no commitments and you can cancel at any time, effective at the end of your current payment period.',
    'faq.q7':'Can I share my account with family?','faq.a7':'Yes — each account supports up to 2 profiles, plus a dedicated PIN-protected Kids profile.',
    'faq.q8':'Will there be subtitles?','faq.a8':'Yes. English subtitles and closed captions are available across the catalogue, with more regional languages planned.',
    'faq.q9':'How do I get support?','faq.a9':'Through a direct WhatsApp customer line — real people, no call centres. Details will be published at launch.',
    'faq.q10':'Which countries will it be available in?','faq.a10':'The entire Southern Africa region: South Africa, Lesotho, Eswatini, Botswana, Mozambique, Namibia, Zimbabwe, Zambia, Malawi and Angola.',

